+# Check PlaceBlock arguments with t
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t` from Wally) at
+  version 3.1.1. Like our other packages, it comes in through pesde and is pinned exactly. Code
+  requires it as `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`. The same validator style can be used for
+  the remotes we add later.
+- Changes the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` to check
+  its arguments with one `t.tuple` validator instead of the hand-written checks.
+- Adds t to the package table in `README.md`.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+Every check the handler made before is still made, in the same order:
+
+| Before | After |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName)`: a value matches only if it equals one of the string keys, so anything that isn't a string fails |
+| `BlockTypes.ByName[blockTypeName]` is nil | Also `t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName)`. `ByName` is frozen when the module loads, so building the literal set once is safe |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` (t defines it as `t.typeof("Vector3")`) |
+| `position ~= position` (NaN component) | Custom `notNaN` check, joined to `t.Vector3` with `t.intersection` |
+
+The rate limit, character/HumanoidRootPart, `Y < 0`, occupied-cell and reach checks come after
+argument checking and are unchanged. As before, extra arguments are ignored: `t.tuple` only checks
+the positions it was given. Invalid calls are still dropped silently.
+
+## Before testing
+
+1. **Install packages:** run `pesde install` from the repo root. This change edits `pesde.toml`
+   only. `t` is not in `roblox_packages/` yet, and `pesde.lock` has not been regenerated, because
+   installs couldn't be run when this was written. Until you install, `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`
+   doesn't exist and `BlockPlacement` will error on require.
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** that the install produces, and push it to this branch so the
+   lockfile matches `pesde.toml`.
+3. **Run the static checks** from the README (none have been run on this change yet):
+   ```sh
+   rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+   luau-lsp analyze --platform=roblox --definitions:@roblox=globalTypes.d.luau --sourcemap=sourcemap.json --ignore=**/roblox_packages/** src
+   selene src
+   stylua --check src
+   ```
+
+## Testing in Studio
+
+Sync with `rojo serve`, start a play session, and from the client command bar:
+
+- `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick", <a position near you>)` places a block.
+- The following should place nothing and raise no server error:
+  - `FireServer("NotABlock", pos)`
+  - `FireServer(123, pos)`
+  - `FireServer("Brick", "pos")`
+  - `FireServer("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))`
+  - `FireServer("Brick")`
